est outcome.\n*   Play Single King: I might not. Worst outcome.\n\nI double-check my hand and valid moves.  It all lines up.  Play the pair!\n\nFinally, I think about this: Does it matter that my teammate has cards? No. My goal is to play out my cards.  I\'m good to go.\n\n**Answer:** `{"cards": ["♠K", "♦K"]}`\n\nThere, done. No need to overcomplicate it. Play the pair, win the game, and move on.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: I currently have only two cards left in my hand, which form a pair of Kings (♠K ♦K). I have a Free Play (control of the board), meaning I can play any valid combination. The objective of the game for a Peasant is to empty their hand before the Landlord.\n\nReason: By playing the pair of Kings, I will successfully play out all my cards and immediately win the game for the Peasant team. There is no benefit to holding back or breaking the pair, as doing so would delay victory and risk the Landlord regaining control.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠K", "♦K"]}'}
